  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nSimple interest = 4347\n\nTime = 7frac23 years = 23/3 years\n\nRate = 5.4% per annum\n\nNew rate = 7.5% per annum\n\nNew time = 4(4)/(5) years = 24/5 years\n\n**Formula Used:**\n\nSI = (P × R × T) ÷ 100\n\nAmount = P + SI\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ 4347 = (P × 5.4 × 23/3) ÷ 100\n\n⇒ 4347 = (P × 5.4 × 23) ÷ 300\n\n⇒ 4347 = (124.2P) ÷ 300\n\n⇒ P = (4347 × 300) ÷ 124.2\n\n⇒ P = 13,04,100 ÷ 124.2\n\n⇒ P = 10,500\n\nNow find new SI:\n\n⇒ SI = (10,500 × 7.5 × 24/5) ÷ 100\n\n⇒ 24/5 = 4.8\n\n⇒ SI = (10,500 × 7.5 × 4.8) ÷ 100\n\n⇒ 7.5 × 4.8 = 36\n\n⇒ SI = (10,500 × 36) ÷ 100\n\n⇒ SI = 3,78,000 ÷ 100\n\n⇒ SI = 3,780\n\n⇒ Amount = 10,500 + 3,780 = 14,280\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 14280.**",
